# Single source of truth

Start of every turn: `AGENTS.md` → `field-guide/index.md` → `docs/architecture/STATUS.md` → `docs/reviews/BOARD.md`. Handshake: `DEC-066-AGENTS`. Ranking: `DEC-066-INDEX`. Human science: `docs/methodology.md`.

- If `STATUS.code_freeze` is true, do not write Python unless the user unfreezes.
- Parent proposes. Two independent sub-agents write `review-a` / `review-b` in parallel (do not read each other). Dual `accept` → implement the named stages; no third review.
- User **build** / **build and execute**: run propose → board → execute through all licensed stages. `build_licensed` is false until that command.
- Rubber-stamp reviews are invalid. New `DEC-*` ids are user-only.
- Commit and push `origin/dev` after propose, tally, and each stage deliverable.
- Cursor `~/.cursor/plans/*.plan.md` is not canon unless it headers `canon_generation` matching STATUS.
- Physics lives in `docs/decisions/DEC-*.md`. Do not paste ADR essays into this rule.
